1
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:43,930
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,940
[Episode 13]

3
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,520
What do you mean?

4
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:57,070
So this is our last dinner together.

5
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,940
Do you have to put it like that?

6
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,560
I shouldn't have bothered
asking you to come back.

7
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,090
You're leaving again
after such a short time.

8
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,900
Where are you going this time?

9
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:15,910
Haven't decided yet.

10
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,520
Basically somewhere in the South, eh?

11
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:24,480
Pretty much.

12
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,120
Have you noticed?

13
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:35,120
Summer here is pretty nice.

14
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:37,290
It's not as hot as it is down South.

15
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,490
I should probably warn you.

16
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,120
If you come back next time,

17
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,710
give me a heads-up first.

18
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,360
I'll be very busy then.

19
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,430
I'm job-hunting right now, remember?

20
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:58,290
I'll be swamped with work by then.

21
00:02:59,079 --> 00:03:00,120
I'll be swamped.

22
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,590
Y-You might not even get to see me.

23
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:02,240
Maybe...

24
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,030
Maybe I won't have time to see you.

25
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:05,630
Let me know in advance, okay?

26
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:07,190
Fine, Boss Liu.

27
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:10,160
I'll let you know
before I come back next time.

28
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,500
I just remembered something.

29
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:22,310
I just remembered.

30
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:24,030
Do you remember when we were kids?

31
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:25,240
Every time you were about to leave,

32
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:27,040
you'd secretly cry in your room.

33
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:28,190
Remember?

34
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,150
You must have your wires crossed.

35
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:30,960
When did I ever cry?

36
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,079
Oh, cut it out.

37
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,000
You and Mom,

38
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:36,240
each hiding in your own room, crying.

39
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,680
I saw it several times.

40
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,470
But I do admit one thing.

41
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,440
You really are a lot like Mom.

42
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:46,320
Very strong-minded.

43
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,120
Especially when something happens,

44
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,920
neither of you tells anyone.
You just tough it out.

45
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,190
When Mom was sick...

46
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,420
she wouldn't let me tell you,
no matter what.

47
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:14,630
That's quite funny.

48
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:16,000
I stayed with Mom

49
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,040
all those years,

50
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,190
yet I didn't turn out like her.

51
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,190
You did.

52
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,510
How come?

53
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,480
How come?

54
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:27,680
You take after Dad, that's why.

55
00:04:32,190 --> 00:04:33,270
What was Dad like?

56
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,380
He had a good personality.

57
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,920
Always cheerful.

58
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:47,830
That explains it.

59
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:49,159
I've always

60
00:04:49,159 --> 00:04:50,720
wondered why I'm so lovable.

61
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,180
Turns out I take after Dad.

62
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:53,360
That's good.

63
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,409
But you used to cry a lot as a kid too.

64
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,680
You cried a lot as a kid,

65
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:01,800
and you still do.

66
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:03,830
Once you start, you just can't stop.

67
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:05,630
Wait.

68
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:07,920
How come...

69
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:08,870
How come I...

70
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,430
c-cry a lot now?

71
00:05:11,510 --> 00:05:13,310
Y-You have plenty of flaws too.

72
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:14,070
You're annoying.

73
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:14,920
You're the annoying type,

74
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,680
through and through.

75
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,040
You've been annoying since childhood,

76
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,160
and somehow you've gotten

77
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,890
even more annoying as an adult.

78
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:21,600
I'm telling you,

79
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,720
I find you so irritating now.

80
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,120
You have no idea how much.

81
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,390
Can you tell that I find you annoying?

82
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:25,800
J-Just

83
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,240
seeing you every day
drives me up the wall.

84
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,160
I-I really...

85
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,040
I-I can barely...

86
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,110
s-stand being

87
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:32,680
around you anymore.

88
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,950
H-Hurry up and leave.

89
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:55,290
If you ever leave Fucheng,

90
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,730
you can come find me.

91
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:07,910
♪ Some say goodbye so easily ♪

92
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,040
Forget it.

93
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:07,990
I'm not going.

94
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,570
I'm not going anywhere.

95
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:15,390
♪ Yet take forever to let go ♪

96
00:06:11,390 --> 00:06:12,990
Staying here is pretty nice.

97
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:25,510
♪ Some smile as they close the door ♪

98
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,850
Don't just eat meat.

99
00:06:26,330 --> 00:06:32,750
♪ Yet turn away with tears in their eyes ♪

100
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,390
Huang.

101
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:47,150
[Xiamen Kaoliang Liquor]

102
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,120
Although we have

103
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,159
different personalities,
don't see eye to eye,

104
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:51,560
and probably won't see each other again...

105
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,159
Um, well...

106
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:54,600
This is a type of sorghum liquor

107
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,630
from Fujian.

108
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:57,120
An older colleague of mine
at my previous workplace

109
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,050
really liked it,

110
00:06:58,390 --> 00:06:59,159
so I ordered

111
00:06:59,159 --> 00:07:00,430
a bottle online for you.

112
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:01,360
Give it a try.

113
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,000
Thank you then.

114
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:08,070
Dr. Che.

115
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,510
Here.

116
00:07:09,830 --> 00:07:10,690
This is for you.

117
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,530
It's a reading list I put together,

118
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,310
along with some papers

119
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:15,430
whose research frameworks I think

120
00:07:15,430 --> 00:07:16,830
are worth learning from.

121
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:18,430
And here...

122
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,270
is the phone number
of one of my classmates.

123
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:21,120
He specializes in

124
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,240
tutoring for
doctoral exams and applications.

125
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,500
He's really good at it.

126
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:25,360
But he...

127
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:27,600
and I don't really get along,

128
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,600
so you don't need to mention my name.

129
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:30,760
You're leaving?

130
00:07:35,070 --> 00:07:36,159
If you have any questions

131
00:07:36,159 --> 00:07:37,600
about anything on this list,

132
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:39,159
just compile them all

133
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:40,360
and send me a message.

134
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:42,870
Thank you.

135
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,190
When you go back to the South,

136
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:50,720
take good care of yourself.

137
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:56,480
"The fish roam the vast sea,

138
00:07:57,870 --> 00:08:00,470
and the birds soar through
the boundless sky."

139
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,620
I hate to see you go.

140
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:06,880
But I'm happy for you.

141
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:17,370
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to
erase the past ♪

142
00:08:13,530 --> 00:08:18,930
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

143
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:26,300
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

144
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:26,440
[Buddhist Scriptures, Joss Paper, Coffins,
Refrigerated casket]

145
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,870
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

146
00:08:27,990 --> 00:08:30,940
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

147
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:35,330
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

148
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:44,030
♪ Maybe walking side by side
for a while is enough ♪

149
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:48,850
[Fortune]

150
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:52,880
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to
erase the past ♪

151
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:49,550
Nice.

152
00:08:54,970 --> 00:09:01,860
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

153
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:06,480
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

154
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:10,970
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

155
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:19,610
♪ Maybe walking side by side
for a while is enough ♪

156
00:09:12,870 --> 00:09:13,670
San.

157
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:15,720
I...

158
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,850
I think I just saw Liu Zhengliang here.

159
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,030
What?

160
00:09:22,670 --> 00:09:23,730
I don't see anyone.

161
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,360
Patient Wang Zongqi's

162
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,910
post-op recovery is normal.

163
00:09:28,910 --> 00:09:29,750
Still under observation,

164
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,150
nothing special needed.

165
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:32,930
That's the nursing handover.

166
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,150
Over to the doctors.

167
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:36,390
The nurses' handover was detailed,

168
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,340
and the additions were thorough.

169
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:39,320
One more thing:

170
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:40,550
today is Chief Physician Liu's

171
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:41,670
last shift.

172
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:42,550
That's all.

173
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,150
Are you really not going to give yourself

174
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,320
a chance?

175
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,200
Once he leaves, he will never come back.

176
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:21,610
[Gastric Lavage Room] [ECG Room]

177
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,120
Dr. Liu.

178
00:10:24,980 --> 00:10:27,220
[No smoking]

179
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:32,840
[Quiet]

180
00:10:31,550 --> 00:10:32,470
Dr. Liu.

181
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:35,790
Dr. Liu.

182
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:25,720
That day,

183
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,750
Zhang Jiao sat beside me

184
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,840
and smiled at me.

185
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:35,150
Only I knew

186
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:37,030
that I walked away

187
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,720
much more slowly than I'd imagined.

188
00:11:56,470 --> 00:12:04,270
[Yellow Zone]

189
00:11:58,630 --> 00:11:59,550
Dr. Liu.

190
00:12:01,910 --> 00:12:02,750
Um,

191
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,670
we heard you're leaving.

192
00:12:05,150 --> 00:12:05,870
This is

193
00:12:05,870 --> 00:12:08,080
a small token of appreciation
from my husband and me.

194
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:10,600
We hope everything goes well for you
in the future.

195
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:11,750
I can't accept this.

196
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,000
I'm not good with words,

197
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,550
and I don't know
how to express myself well.

198
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,480
But I know

199
00:12:17,790 --> 00:12:19,000
that without you,

200
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,000
Jiao wouldn't have made it this far,

201
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,060
nor would she have recovered so well.

202
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:24,270
Besides,

203
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:24,790
you've helped us

204
00:12:24,790 --> 00:12:26,790
save a lot of money on medical bills.

205
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:29,440
Today is your last day

206
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,770
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

207
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:32,240
Her dad and I

208
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:34,360
didn't know what to get you.

209
00:12:34,750 --> 00:12:36,350
It's meant purely as thanks.

210
00:12:36,510 --> 00:12:37,510
We're just afraid that if we don't

211
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:39,790
thank you now,
we might not get another chance.

212
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:40,840
Please accept it.

213
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:42,670
The hospital has rules.

214
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:44,070
I really can't accept it.

215
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:47,360
Just...

216
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,320
Just think of it as a gift from Jiao.

217
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:53,350
You can buy yourself
something to eat or drink on the road.

218
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,550
Please accept it.

219
00:13:00,390 --> 00:13:01,080
Okay.

220
00:13:04,910 --> 00:13:05,720
I'm going.

221
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:22,180
[Guide for Patients
with Out-of-Area Insurance]

222
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:22,440
Um, here.

223
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:22,370
[Priority for acute stroke patients
and patients aged 80 and older.]

224
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,320
Please deposit this

225
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,850
into Zhang Jiao's account.

226
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,340
-Okay, Chief Physician Liu.
-Thank you.

227
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:32,000
[Thank you, Dr. Liu Zhengliang,
for saving Zhang Jiao.]

228
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,210
[May you always be safe and sound,
and may everything go well for you.]

229
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:44,870
He'll be right out.

230
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:57,910
I can't take you to the station now.

231
00:13:57,910 --> 00:13:58,720
Something came up at home.

232
00:13:58,720 --> 00:13:59,630
Call me, okay?

233
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:00,150
What the heck?

234
00:14:00,150 --> 00:14:01,200
I gotta go.

235
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:05,630
[Emergency]

236
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:11,000
What's with him?

237
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,630
Three.

238
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:15,320
Two.

239
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,000
One.

240
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,130
[West Gate]

241
00:14:47,130 --> 00:14:49,830
[Fucheng City Public Security Bureau
Hospital Police Post]

242
00:15:11,550 --> 00:15:12,950
You were just gonna leave

243
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,980
without so much as a word, huh?

244
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:17,840
Here, you have the soda.

245
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:20,600
I'll have a beer.

246
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,000
Cheers.

247
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:28,770
"Come, drink one last cup of wine with me.

248
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,370
Beyond Yang Pass,
no old friends you'll see."

249
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:32,790
Cheers.

250
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,840
Don't forget me when you get to the South.

251
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,370
How could I ever forget you?

252
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,790
I mean,

253
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:06,950
you're very special.

254
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,460
You're not easy to forget.

255
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:12,240
I've never met

256
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,500
anyone quite like you.

257
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,880
What kind of person am I?

258
00:16:45,150 --> 00:16:46,510
I'm this kind of person.

259
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,510
No.

260
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,530
I'm going back to the South.

261
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:09,440
Good, then I won't have to
be responsible for you anymore.

262
00:17:13,589 --> 00:17:14,750
I-I'm very poor.

263
00:17:15,109 --> 00:17:16,550
Who freaking cares?

264
00:17:19,349 --> 00:17:20,410
I have a condition.

265
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,460
I-I have a snow phobia.

266
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,260
I have a condition too.

267
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:38,200
I can't read.

268
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,680
Are you sure you're taking the train?

269
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:57,000
[East Zhanqian Road]

270
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:58,410
Why not fly the day after tomorrow?

271
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:00,440
The train's cheaper.

272
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:02,400
Fine.

273
00:18:03,750 --> 00:18:04,750
I got the tickets.

274
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,270
Check the tickets carefully.

275
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:07,510
The first one gets you to

276
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,600
[Fucheng to Nanjing]

277
00:18:07,510 --> 00:18:08,350
Nanjing tonight.

278
00:18:08,350 --> 00:18:10,070
The second one
gets you to Fuzhou tomorrow.

279
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,790
[Nanjing to Fuzhou]

280
00:18:10,070 --> 00:18:11,070
Don't mix them up.

281
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:15,040
You're solid.

282
00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:16,200
Five stars, would use again.

283
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,160
Together, they cost
a little over 700 yuan.

284
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,220
That's 300 yuan cheaper than flying.

285
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,740
But that's 2 extra days of suffering.

286
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:24,240
Three hundred isn't nothing.

287
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:24,960
I've only managed to save up

288
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,960
9,000 yuan over the past few months.

289
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:28,240
Every little bit counts.

290
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,270
Didn't Aunt Ling

291
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:30,870
leave some money for you two?

292
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,330
Zhengguang didn't give you yours, did he?

293
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:35,440
He did.

294
00:18:35,510 --> 00:18:36,440
I didn't take it.

295
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,790
You've learned to
look out for your little brother.

296
00:18:38,790 --> 00:18:40,030
It's not that.

297
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:42,680
At first, I was definitely

298
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:44,010
going to take the money.

299
00:18:44,550 --> 00:18:46,280
But when I went home last night,

300
00:18:46,590 --> 00:18:48,450
I saw him eating instant noodles.

301
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:51,120
You went home last night?

302
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:55,570
What's wrong with that?

303
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:56,960
Nothing.

304
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:57,830
And then?

305
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:00,590
Anyway,

306
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:01,850
I just changed my mind.

307
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,300
I'm leaving the money for him.

308
00:19:04,590 --> 00:19:06,650
You know what Liu Zhengguang is like.

309
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:08,310
He's not the brightest
and doesn't have much going for him.

310
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:09,510
I'm afraid he won't find a job

311
00:19:09,510 --> 00:19:11,510
and will literally starve to death.

312
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:15,220
You're being so generous, yet you're

313
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:17,480
still trying to save money on airfare.

314
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:19,410
I don't think you're saving money.

315
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,930
I think you're dodging a debt, huh?

316
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,070
Nonsense.

317
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:26,100
How could I ever be in debt?

318
00:19:53,380 --> 00:20:04,630
[Contactless Payment;
No Stopping Required]

319
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:04,920
Be careful.

320
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:07,180
No need to walk me any farther. I'm going.

321
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:09,460
You're just trying to avoid Ai Chen, huh?

322
00:20:11,310 --> 00:20:12,240
No such thing.

323
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:15,000
There's nothing between Ai Chen and me.

324
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,510
We're just ordinary friends.

325
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:17,310
No,

326
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:18,920
just ordinary acquaintances.

327
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,200
I haven't even asked you anything,

328
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,530
and you're already giving yourself away.

329
00:20:28,790 --> 00:20:30,390
Alright, this is far enough.

330
00:20:30,750 --> 00:20:33,160
I'll keep in touch online
once I get there.

331
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,830
Once you leave,

332
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,640
we'll go from colleagues

333
00:20:40,270 --> 00:20:41,730
and childhood friends...

334
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:44,210
to just online friends.

335
00:20:49,270 --> 00:20:50,270
Take care.

336
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:08,030
You too.

337
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:12,920
-Everyone, tuck your feet in.
-Thank you.

338
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,110
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

339
00:21:14,110 --> 00:21:14,880
Where're our berths?

340
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,410
Excuse me, coming through.

341
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:17,240
Here.

342
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:17,830
This one?

343
00:21:17,830 --> 00:21:18,240
Here.

344
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,170
Watch your feet.

345
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:20,550
Excuse me.

346
00:21:22,510 --> 00:21:23,550
Whose shoes are these?

347
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:24,350
Move them in a bit.

348
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:25,750
Watch your feet. Thanks.

349
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:27,880
Don't block the aisle.

350
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:28,680
Okay, okay.

351
00:21:32,590 --> 00:21:33,750
Thanks. Come on.

352
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:39,160
Okay, thanks.

353
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:39,820
No problem.

354
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:43,510
What, is your suitcase hard to push?

355
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:44,350
Push harder.

356
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:45,920
You're a man. Push harder.

357
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,510
Okay, thanks.

358
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:47,240
Okay, okay.

359
00:21:48,510 --> 00:21:49,710
Set it down securely.

360
00:21:52,310 --> 00:21:53,910
Everyone, pull your feet in.

361
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,110
Liu Zhengliang is leaving today,

362
00:21:57,110 --> 00:21:57,920
you know?

363
00:21:58,110 --> 00:21:58,790
I know.

364
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:02,400
He lied to me
and said he was leaving tonight.

365
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,510
I just called Junnan, and he said

366
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:05,200
Zhengliang's already on the train now.

367
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:05,790
What?

368
00:22:05,790 --> 00:22:07,590
You came j-just to tell me this?

369
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:12,110
I was afraid you didn't know.

370
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,370
What does it matter if I know or not?

371
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,510
Was I supposed to
throw myself on the floor, make a scene,

372
00:22:16,510 --> 00:22:17,270
and stop him from leaving?

373
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:18,510
Why stop him?

374
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,270
Didn't I tell you, Chen?

375
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,270
You two aren't right for each other.

376
00:22:21,270 --> 00:22:22,440
Yeah, who could possibly be right

377
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:23,400
for a guy like him?

378
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:24,270
Exactly.

379
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:25,310
The person who's right for him

380
00:22:25,310 --> 00:22:27,110
doesn't even exist in this world.

381
00:22:27,110 --> 00:22:28,510
He deserves to die alone.

382
00:22:28,590 --> 00:22:30,450
What did he say about me back then?

383
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,640
He said I wasn't good enough for him.

384
00:22:34,030 --> 00:22:35,510
I'm not good enough for him?

385
00:22:35,510 --> 00:22:36,750
No, Chen, I was there that day.

386
00:22:36,750 --> 00:22:37,680
When h-he said that,

387
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,310
I was there.

388
00:22:38,310 --> 00:22:38,680
Right.

389
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,350
At the hospital.

390
00:22:39,350 --> 00:22:40,590
You were there.

391
00:22:40,590 --> 00:22:41,750
He said you weren't good enough for him.

392
00:22:41,750 --> 00:22:44,080
If you ask me,
he's not good enough for you.

393
00:22:44,110 --> 00:22:45,550
You know, here's the thing:

394
00:22:45,550 --> 00:22:46,680
good looks have no ceiling,

395
00:22:46,680 --> 00:22:48,280
but insecurity has no floor.

396
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:49,960
That's what I've been saying.

397
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,560
He seems a bit insecure to me.

398
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,790
Chen,

399
00:22:53,070 --> 00:22:54,680
you've hit the nail on the head.

400
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:55,350
Right?

401
00:22:55,510 --> 00:22:57,200
People like him might seem

402
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,270
cold and aloof on the outside,

403
00:22:58,270 --> 00:22:59,270
like they're full of confidence.

404
00:22:59,270 --> 00:23:01,480
But often, they're more insecure inside.

405
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:02,270
Sometimes I wonder

406
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:03,590
how to describe a guy like him.

407
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,200
He's...

408
00:23:05,070 --> 00:23:05,920
He's just like tofu,

409
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:06,680
you know?

410
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,680
Such a pushover.

411
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:11,920
Good thing he didn't
go to school in the Northeast.

412
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:12,590
If he had,

413
00:23:12,590 --> 00:23:13,720
he'd have been beaten up 8 times a day.

414
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,640
Tell me about it.

415
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:15,640
He's asking for a beating.

416
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,750
He's begging for one.

417
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:17,480
But you have to admit,

418
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,720
he was a good student.

419
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,270
So what if he was a good student?

420
00:23:20,270 --> 00:23:21,550
Does that make him better
at taking a beating?

421
00:23:21,550 --> 00:23:23,350
He would get special treatment.

422
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:25,440
Isn't that how it always is around here?

423
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,240
True.

424
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:28,550
E-Even so, he'd still get beaten up.

425
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:29,610
He loved to snitch.

426
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:30,810
What do you mean?

427
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,310
Remember when we were kids
and we'd make dumplings for the New Year?

428
00:23:33,310 --> 00:23:35,240
We'd put coins inside some of them.

429
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,240
And I'd want to eat the ones with coins.

430
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:37,680
So I'd poke them with chopsticks

431
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,000
to find the hard ones.

432
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,790
I'd poke them full of holes.

433
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,270
Then he'd turn around and tell Mom.

434
00:23:42,270 --> 00:23:43,030
He did?

435
00:23:43,270 --> 00:23:45,200
Mom'd come back and give me a beating.

436
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,350
You deserved it.

437
00:23:47,070 --> 00:23:48,160
That's true.

438
00:23:48,790 --> 00:23:50,240
But I used to do that too.

439
00:23:52,110 --> 00:23:53,160
Just poking them.

440
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,920
Chen, when do you think

441
00:24:13,310 --> 00:24:14,770
he'll come back this time?

442
00:24:16,750 --> 00:24:17,750
Hard to say.

443
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,480
Let him go if he wants to.

444
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:24,010
As if anyone wants him back.

445
00:24:24,550 --> 00:24:26,030
How's your job hunt going?

446
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,720
It's going great.

447
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:31,030
Loads of people are fighting to hire me.

448
00:24:31,030 --> 00:24:32,510
I have to take my time to choose.

449
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:33,910
Look at you, so in demand.

450
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:37,050
Just don't get dazzled by all the options.

451
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:40,110
If there's nothing else, I'll get going.

452
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:40,920
Go on back.

453
00:24:41,110 --> 00:24:42,750
Drink some hot water. Don't catch a cold.

454
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:43,480
It's pretty cold out here.

455
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:44,480
I'll head inside in a bit.

456
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:45,110
Bye-bye.

457
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,310
You smoke?

458
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:30,920
I started really young.

459
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:32,180
But I don't smoke much.

460
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,970
You didn't know I smoke?

461
00:25:34,590 --> 00:25:35,720
Never saw it before.

462
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,830
You're not going to tell me

463
00:25:38,830 --> 00:25:39,750
that smoking is bad for my health

464
00:25:39,750 --> 00:25:41,480
and that I should quit, are you?

465
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:43,310
Your body, your choice.

466
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:54,110
But honestly, it's hard for me to imagine

467
00:25:54,110 --> 00:25:55,440
that in this day and age,

468
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:57,970
there are still young people
who can't read.

469
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,460
I have a reading disorder.

470
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,240
But it's not like

471
00:26:05,550 --> 00:26:07,480
I can't recognize any characters at all.

472
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:08,640
I'd say I know about

473
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:10,770
one-tenth of all Chinese characters.

474
00:26:11,350 --> 00:26:12,720
That sounds like

475
00:26:13,070 --> 00:26:15,200
abnormal neurological development.

476
00:26:16,270 --> 00:26:17,720
Have you ever seen a doctor about it?

477
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:19,520
Other than that one time with me.

478
00:26:20,750 --> 00:26:21,880
I've had it checked.

479
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:24,690
It's not a neurological issue.

480
00:26:25,070 --> 00:26:25,960
Then what is it?

481
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:38,440
I dropped out in fifth grade.

482
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,360
How is that possible?

483
00:26:41,310 --> 00:26:43,110
We have 9-year compulsory education.

484
00:26:43,110 --> 00:26:45,030
And we Northeasterners
take education so seriously.

485
00:26:45,030 --> 00:26:46,890
My family situation was unusual.

486
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:50,660
I didn't start third grade until I was 11.

487
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:54,770
I've had trouble reading
since I was a kid.

488
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,030
So my parents were afraid I'd be

489
00:26:57,030 --> 00:26:58,510
-looked down on at school.
-What's

490
00:26:58,510 --> 00:26:59,440
this character?

491
00:26:59,550 --> 00:27:01,160
So they taught me at home.

492
00:27:01,850 --> 00:27:08,290
[Be Late; After School; Home]

493
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,960
I just taught you this yesterday,

494
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:13,070
and you've already forgotten it?

495
00:27:13,070 --> 00:27:14,160
What's my name?

496
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:18,830
What did we have for lunch?

497
00:27:20,880 --> 00:27:21,720
Rice.

498
00:27:22,790 --> 00:27:23,680
Smart girl.

499
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:24,590
See?

500
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:26,760
Then what's this character?

501
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:29,830
Rice.

502
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:31,480
Smart girl.

503
00:27:32,110 --> 00:27:32,920
Remember it.

504
00:27:34,590 --> 00:27:35,920
Write it a few more times.

505
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:36,720
Ai San!

506
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:38,310
Coming! Coming!

507
00:27:38,310 --> 00:27:39,920
Write it a-a few more times.

508
00:27:41,510 --> 00:27:42,310
Keep writing.

509
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,100
Write it again.

510
00:27:47,720 --> 00:27:49,050
Do you know why I'm here?

511
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:54,270
You dared to steal the antique

512
00:27:54,270 --> 00:27:56,240
belonging to a Hong Kong businessman?

513
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,370
Where did you put it?

514
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,640
B-Bring it out.

515
00:27:59,790 --> 00:28:01,000
That's a collectible.

516
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,200
Worth a fortune.

517
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:06,480
That was the first time I learned

518
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:09,590
my mom had kleptomania.

519
00:28:10,960 --> 00:28:12,690
She couldn't control herself.

520
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,680
Tell me, who did it?

521
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:25,310
Me.

522
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:29,890
With your hand injured like that,

523
00:28:30,030 --> 00:28:32,160
you still managed such delicate work?

524
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:35,270
I-It didn't get in the way.

525
00:28:38,350 --> 00:28:39,210
Alright, then.

526
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:40,740
You, come back with us.

527
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:43,270
Ai Chen, I'm leaving.

528
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:46,960
Dad!

529
00:28:52,590 --> 00:28:53,650
Listen to your mom.

530
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:56,540
My dad went to jail just like that.

531
00:28:58,310 --> 00:29:00,160
The court ruled
that the amount involved was huge,

532
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:01,890
so he was sentenced to 10 years.

533
00:29:04,790 --> 00:29:08,110
Later, my mom got a job

534
00:29:08,790 --> 00:29:10,520
at a hospital through a friend,

535
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:11,590
doing odd jobs.

536
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:15,800
But she didn't last long.

537
00:29:16,110 --> 00:29:17,110
Her kleptomania acted up again,

538
00:29:17,110 --> 00:29:18,910
and they fired her immediately.

539
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:28,480
Mi Si.

540
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,000
She had no choice.

541
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:37,070
She had to raise me.

542
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:39,750
So she thought...

543
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:42,440
why not go to the train station

544
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:44,040
and return to her old tricks?

545
00:29:44,540 --> 00:29:46,510
[Passenger Travel Guidelines]

546
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,270
Little did she know,

547
00:29:46,510 --> 00:29:47,090
[Our Service Promise]

548
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:50,340
that the police
had been watching her all along.

549
00:30:04,750 --> 00:30:05,810
And just like that,

550
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,220
my mom went to jail too.

551
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,480
I was left all alone,

552
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:12,970
with no one to depend on.

553
00:30:15,030 --> 00:30:17,350
Uncle Li, the police officer,

554
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,320
took pity on me and took me in.

555
00:30:21,590 --> 00:30:22,400
Xiaozhu?

556
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:23,510
Xiaozhu.

557
00:30:25,310 --> 00:30:26,960
This is your sister, Chen.

558
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:28,970
This is my son, Xiaozhu.

559
00:30:29,830 --> 00:30:31,360
Treat this as your own home.

560
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:50,160
Hot dumplings coming up!

561
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:52,640
Here.

562
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:53,750
Alright.

563
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:55,790
Eat slowly. Don't burn yourself.

564
00:30:55,790 --> 00:30:56,440
Come on.

565
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,550
Try the dumplings I made.

566
00:30:59,310 --> 00:31:00,920
One for you. One for you.

567
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,160
Eat up.

568
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:08,290
Why wouldn't your mom
let you go to school?

569
00:31:08,310 --> 00:31:10,720
She said learning at home
was just as good.

570
00:31:11,310 --> 00:31:12,350
Nonsense.

571
00:31:13,270 --> 00:31:14,930
She was only holding you back.

572
00:31:24,310 --> 00:31:26,970
Xiaozhu, you've learned to
take care of others.

573
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:27,920
Eat up.

574
00:31:37,310 --> 00:31:38,160
Hand it over.

575
00:31:38,510 --> 00:31:40,070
Or we'll beat you up.

576
00:31:41,160 --> 00:31:42,000
Give it here.

577
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,880
Hurry up!

578
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:44,960
Hand it over.

579
00:31:44,960 --> 00:31:46,240
I'll say it again.

580
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,100
Give it to us, or we'll beat you up!

581
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:48,960
Hurry!

582
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:50,790
Hurry up!

583
00:31:58,640 --> 00:31:59,480
You're asking for it.

584
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:00,510
I'll kill you.

585
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:01,750
Li Xiaozhu!

586
00:32:05,510 --> 00:32:06,310
This is my little brother.

587
00:32:06,310 --> 00:32:07,750
Get along well with him from now on,

588
00:32:07,750 --> 00:32:09,350
and I'll buy you more snacks.

589
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:11,000
I want this one.

590
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:11,680
This big one.

591
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:11,960
Okay.

592
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:12,680
Let's go.

593
00:32:14,310 --> 00:32:15,030
It's okay.

594
00:32:15,070 --> 00:32:16,920
From now on, Sis has your back.

595
00:32:19,790 --> 00:32:21,050
Come on, let's go home.

596
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:29,810
Xiaozhu and I were both mischievous.

597
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:31,000
Back then,

598
00:32:31,640 --> 00:32:33,100
he was my little sidekick.

599
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:35,550
And me? I was the boss, naturally.

600
00:32:39,030 --> 00:32:40,960
He was in third grade,

601
00:32:41,480 --> 00:32:42,350
so Uncle Li

602
00:32:42,350 --> 00:32:43,550
put me straight

603
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,160
into his class

604
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:47,020
so we could go to school together.

605
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,780
Strangely enough,

606
00:32:51,640 --> 00:32:53,640
I was very good at memorizing texts—

607
00:32:53,750 --> 00:32:55,680
classical poems and verses.

608
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:57,480
I was okay at math too.

609
00:32:58,310 --> 00:33:00,040
But when it came to characters,

610
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:02,160
I just couldn't remember them.

611
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:02,920
So back then,

612
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:04,200
both my teacher and Uncle Li thought

613
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:06,330
I was deliberately refusing to learn.

614
00:33:06,350 --> 00:33:07,400
How could they have known

615
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:09,060
that I had a reading disorder?

616
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:11,070
But I didn't know at the time either.

617
00:33:11,070 --> 00:33:13,000
I only found out later,
when I saw a doctor.

618
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:15,160
The doctor said,
"Why didn't you come earlier,

619
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,360
when you were little?

620
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:17,780
Now it's too late."

621
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:18,640
Ai Chen,

622
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:19,550
what's going on?

623
00:33:19,550 --> 00:33:21,550
Why aren't you doing your homework?

624
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:25,900
Come to my office after class.

625
00:33:27,240 --> 00:33:28,030
Ai Chen,

626
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:30,160
what's this character?

627
00:33:34,270 --> 00:33:35,400
What about this one?

628
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:40,720
She can't read.

629
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,720
She can't read.

630
00:33:42,830 --> 00:33:44,160
What did you just say?

631
00:33:46,030 --> 00:33:46,830
Beat him!

632
00:33:47,750 --> 00:33:49,880
No more bullying classmates at school!

633
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:50,750
Do you hear me?

634
00:33:55,510 --> 00:33:56,510
And you.

635
00:33:57,550 --> 00:33:58,350
Child,

636
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,680
if you don't study hard now,

637
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:01,960
you definitely won't

638
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:04,240
-get into college in the future.
-It wasn't easy for Uncle Li to raise us.

639
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:06,720
What will you do
if you can't get into college?

640
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:08,280
I was afraid
that telling him I had a disorder

641
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,480
would only cause him more trouble,

642
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:10,679
so I kept it to myself.

643
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:13,670
Later, the doctor told me

644
00:34:14,150 --> 00:34:16,080
that if we'd intervened in time...

645
00:34:20,070 --> 00:34:21,929
But there's no changing the past.

646
00:34:26,590 --> 00:34:27,590
Uncle Li...

647
00:34:29,070 --> 00:34:30,600
passed away very suddenly.

648
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,710
After that,

649
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:36,150
it was just Xiaozhu and me.

650
00:34:42,150 --> 00:34:42,920
Mentor!

651
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,480
Mentor, wake up!

652
00:34:44,840 --> 00:34:45,590
Mentor!

653
00:34:48,110 --> 00:34:48,880
Mentor!

654
00:34:53,139 --> 00:34:54,340
[To Li Xiaofeng]

655
00:35:21,060 --> 00:35:24,340
[Forever in Our Hearts]

656
00:35:24,630 --> 00:35:25,590
Li Xiaozhu,

657
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:27,030
stop crying.

658
00:35:27,920 --> 00:35:28,980
Hurry up and think—

659
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,260
do you have any relatives you can rely on?

660
00:35:33,070 --> 00:35:33,710
Didn't you say

661
00:35:33,710 --> 00:35:35,030
your mom went to Shenzhen?

662
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:36,630
Can you get in touch with her?

663
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:37,590
I lied!

664
00:35:37,590 --> 00:35:39,590
I've never even met my mom!

665
00:35:39,590 --> 00:35:40,760
My dad said she ran off

666
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,760
while working abroad that year!

667
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:44,230
She'll never come back!

668
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:45,630
Sis, are we going to

669
00:35:45,630 --> 00:35:47,440
have to beg for food from now on?

670
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:51,920
Since you call me "Sis,"

671
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:52,840
you won't starve

672
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:54,040
as long as I have food.

673
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:00,960
It's all packed.

674
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:02,090
You can take it home.

675
00:36:02,510 --> 00:36:03,670
As for the expenses,

676
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:05,000
Officer Zhang has already paid me.

677
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,000
You don't need to worry about it.

678
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:06,930
I'm heading out.

679
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:07,920
Uncle Sun!

680
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:10,150
Uncle Sun,

681
00:36:10,150 --> 00:36:11,750
I want to be your apprentice.

682
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,150
My apprentice?

683
00:36:13,150 --> 00:36:14,400
What could I teach you?

684
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:16,190
Teach me how to arrange funerals.

685
00:36:16,190 --> 00:36:17,050
Don't be silly.

686
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:18,670
You're just a kid.
You should be in school.

687
00:36:18,670 --> 00:36:19,480
Why get into the funeral business?

688
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:20,630
You can't do this job.

689
00:36:20,630 --> 00:36:21,840
There are no adults left in our family.

690
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:23,360
We have to support ourselves.

691
00:36:23,360 --> 00:36:25,070
People are always coming and going here,

692
00:36:25,070 --> 00:36:26,360
all crying and sobbing.

693
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:27,840
Only you, hiding in the corner,

694
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:28,630
look so happy.

695
00:36:28,630 --> 00:36:29,630
I don't.

696
00:36:30,510 --> 00:36:32,170
When you were counting money.

697
00:36:32,230 --> 00:36:33,510
I saw it all.

698
00:36:33,710 --> 00:36:34,710
I want to make money.

699
00:36:34,710 --> 00:36:35,280
I also want to

700
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:37,140
be happy while others are crying.

701
00:36:38,630 --> 00:36:39,710
Don't talk nonsense here.

702
00:36:39,710 --> 00:36:41,000
This is serious work.

703
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,230
What's all this talk about being happy?

704
00:36:42,230 --> 00:36:43,320
Uncle Sun.

705
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:48,460
What can you do if I take you on?

706
00:36:50,230 --> 00:36:51,150
I can cry.

707
00:36:52,030 --> 00:36:53,800
Since you two will handle funerals
for countless families,

708
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:55,030
using your real names is not appropriate.

709
00:36:55,030 --> 00:36:55,840
I'll give you two

710
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:57,570
stage names for this business.

711
00:36:57,760 --> 00:36:59,070
Li Xiaozhu, you're strong

712
00:36:59,070 --> 00:37:00,000
and chubby.

713
00:37:00,190 --> 00:37:01,710
And your real name means "Pillar."

714
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:03,630
So from now on,
you'll be "Rainbow Pillar."

715
00:37:03,630 --> 00:37:04,800
Ai Chen, you...

716
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,480
Master,

717
00:37:05,630 --> 00:37:07,090
I'll keep my name, Ai Chen.

718
00:37:07,110 --> 00:37:08,440
Both your parents are still alive.

719
00:37:08,440 --> 00:37:09,800
Aren't you worried about bad luck?

720
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:10,760
Every time I do this work,

721
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:11,670
I sincerely hope

722
00:37:11,670 --> 00:37:13,800
the deceased will enjoy a good next life.

723
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:14,840
You said it yourself:

724
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:16,000
in our line of work,

725
00:37:16,150 --> 00:37:17,960
as long as you're sincere,
there's no taboo

726
00:37:17,960 --> 00:37:19,890
to worry about and nothing to fear.

727
00:37:25,070 --> 00:37:26,470
Master, the food is here.

728
00:37:27,230 --> 00:37:28,630
Next time, I'll fetch it.

729
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:30,590
Hurry, sit down and eat.

730
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:31,550
Here, let's eat.

731
00:37:31,410 --> 00:37:34,710
♪ One who nestled close
on a winter's night ♪

732
00:37:35,070 --> 00:37:38,260
♪ A bite of food beside a pool of gaze ♪

733
00:37:38,820 --> 00:37:40,940
♪ When summer dusk arrives ♪

734
00:37:41,380 --> 00:37:43,490
♪ We'll go to see the flowers ♪

735
00:37:45,980 --> 00:37:49,230
♪ One who was stranded on the road ♪

736
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:52,770
♪ Heels buried under unseen snow ♪

737
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:51,670
When I turned 18,

738
00:37:53,260 --> 00:37:55,500
♪ Don't panic—the journey is long ♪

739
00:37:53,280 --> 00:37:54,670
my master taught me

740
00:37:54,670 --> 00:37:55,670
everything he knew,

741
00:37:55,670 --> 00:37:56,590
and then he passed away too.

742
00:37:55,870 --> 00:37:58,390
♪ Long enough to hold your pause ♪

743
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:59,070
After I saw him off on his final journey,

744
00:37:59,070 --> 00:37:59,840
I knew

745
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:03,440
it was time to start my own business.

746
00:38:15,510 --> 00:38:17,320
1314 Funeral Services!

747
00:38:16,410 --> 00:38:20,700
[1314 Funeral Services]

748
00:38:30,530 --> 00:38:32,680
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

749
00:38:31,430 --> 00:38:36,940
[Fucheng City Detention Center]

750
00:38:33,090 --> 00:38:35,890
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

751
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:39,570
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

752
00:38:40,670 --> 00:38:42,070
Later, my mom got out of prison.

753
00:38:41,150 --> 00:38:46,990
♪ Toward the crossroads
brimming with sunlight ♪

754
00:38:42,550 --> 00:38:44,550
So she just started working with me.

755
00:38:45,510 --> 00:38:46,880
However, my mom

756
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:48,590
has no interest

757
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:49,960
in business at all.

758
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:52,250
But she's really good at one thing:

759
00:38:52,510 --> 00:38:53,320
bargaining.

760
00:38:54,070 --> 00:38:55,360
So I brought her on board.

761
00:38:55,360 --> 00:38:57,590
I told her to
be i-in charge of purchasing.

762
00:38:57,590 --> 00:38:58,920
She's really good at it.

763
00:38:59,590 --> 00:39:01,190
My dad is...

764
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:04,670
very handy.

765
00:39:05,670 --> 00:39:06,960
So after he got out,

766
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:08,590
he taught himself how to restore bodies,

767
00:39:08,590 --> 00:39:10,050
do their makeup, and so on.

768
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,510
Xiaozhu and I handle
the funeral ceremonies

769
00:39:12,510 --> 00:39:13,840
and play the suona horn—

770
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:16,060
the whole one-stop funeral service.

771
00:39:17,510 --> 00:39:18,400
Now,

772
00:39:18,550 --> 00:39:21,080
business has been
getting better and better.

773
00:39:22,150 --> 00:39:23,750
I really didn't expect this.

774
00:39:24,110 --> 00:39:25,550
I always assumed you just

775
00:39:26,070 --> 00:39:27,710
took over your father's business.

776
00:39:27,710 --> 00:39:29,770
Turns out, your father joined yours.

777
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:32,360
You could put it that way.

778
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:36,960
Does that bother you?

779
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:41,750
What would bother me?

780
00:39:42,920 --> 00:39:43,920
Why do you think

781
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,320
I'm telling you all this?

782
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:51,920
I should go.

783
00:39:52,230 --> 00:39:53,290
Will you come back?

784
00:39:54,710 --> 00:39:55,440
No.

785
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:58,340
We'll never see each other again?

786
00:39:58,550 --> 00:39:59,760
Probably not.

787
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:03,440
When a-are you leaving?

788
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:04,760
Tomorrow.

789
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:08,670
I have a job tomorrow morning.

790
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:10,230
If you're leaving after noon,

791
00:40:10,230 --> 00:40:11,290
I could see you off.

792
00:40:12,150 --> 00:40:13,190
It's okay. You don't have to.

793
00:40:13,190 --> 00:40:14,280
I'll go by myself.

794
00:40:15,710 --> 00:40:17,110
Will you remember me?

795
00:40:20,110 --> 00:40:21,110
Didn't I just answer

796
00:40:21,110 --> 00:40:22,230
that question?

797
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:29,110
Go.

798
00:40:39,150 --> 00:40:40,280
You're so smart.

799
00:40:40,670 --> 00:40:41,920
You've learned so much

800
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:44,150
just from watching TV
and listening to the radio.

801
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:45,550
That means you don't have

802
00:40:46,550 --> 00:40:47,550
a chronic

803
00:40:48,230 --> 00:40:49,800
neurodegenerative disease

804
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:52,550
or vascular cognitive impairment.

805
00:40:53,070 --> 00:40:53,800
I think your disorder

806
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:55,150
probably stems from a combination

807
00:40:55,150 --> 00:40:56,440
of childhood malnutrition,

808
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:58,630
a difficult upbringing,

809
00:40:58,670 --> 00:41:01,730
psychological avoidance,
and several other factors.

810
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:03,320
Don't laugh. I'm serious.

811
00:41:03,320 --> 00:41:04,630
And look at you now.

812
00:41:04,670 --> 00:41:06,320
Your cognition and development

813
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:07,510
are perfectly intact.

814
00:41:07,510 --> 00:41:08,710
So there's still a high chance

815
00:41:08,710 --> 00:41:10,710
that your condition can be treated.

816
00:41:12,550 --> 00:41:14,030
Aren't you something?

817
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:18,280
You can tell I developed normally
just by looking at me?

818
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,110
Stop dragging this out, will you?

819
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:20,710
If you're leaving, hurry up!

820
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:23,810
Emotional wounds are hard to heal.

821
00:41:24,150 --> 00:41:25,810
You know that better than I do.

822
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:35,240
You're right.

823
00:41:36,150 --> 00:41:37,410
I'm hardly one to talk.

824
00:41:59,000 --> 00:41:59,800
Young man.

825
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:01,670
Young man!

826
00:42:03,590 --> 00:42:04,990
You're traveling alone?

827
00:42:07,550 --> 00:42:08,750
Where are you headed?

828
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:11,230
The last stop.

829
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:13,960
Going to Nanjing on a business trip?

830
00:42:14,230 --> 00:42:14,920
No.

831
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:16,940
I'm going... going to Fuzhou.

832
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,320
That's a long way.

833
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:20,090
Must be a tough journey.

834
00:42:22,510 --> 00:42:24,480
What do you do for a living?

835
00:42:28,150 --> 00:42:29,320
I'm a doctor.

836
00:42:29,920 --> 00:42:31,150
You're a doctor?

837
00:42:31,360 --> 00:42:32,320
Which hospital?

838
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:34,800
Fuzhou Kangtaierke Hospital.

839
00:42:36,630 --> 00:42:38,480
I know Contac.

840
00:42:39,150 --> 00:42:40,280
Kangtaierke?

841
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:41,840
Never heard of it.

842
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,920
So you're heading back

843
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:46,190
after a business trip here.

844
00:42:46,190 --> 00:42:48,250
I thought you were a Northeasterner.

845
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,980
Turns out you're from Fujian.

846
00:42:50,190 --> 00:42:52,320
I can't hear a trace of a Fujian accent.

847
00:42:52,510 --> 00:42:53,800
I'm not from Fujian.

848
00:42:55,110 --> 00:42:56,360
Then where are you from?
